#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186500322 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133848 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5924037a-ddc3-5f50-b4b0-1bd813cef255" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Distance Between a Vector to a Subspace of Solutions of a Linear System"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13c9ab58-bd09-5df1-8d1d-2d4ce831e5f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499698} {:answer/id #uuid "4fda416c-29ab-5041-9567-21fe9188edc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499807} {:answer/id #uuid "6123a26d-2828-5a47-a292-99e6c3705513" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499845} {:answer/id #uuid "bcbbd696-cd17-5e43-a03c-c815bdcc9a15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500039} {:answer/id #uuid "c898ab35-05fd-5fa1-8c7c-3ba6a9711cb3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500064}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6123a26d-2828-5a47-a292-99e6c3705513" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499845} :answer-field/id #uuid "112e9326-3d57-5ecf-afb8-b6f921f35c4c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500187}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "7b37b44d-e7cb-5e9e-b8af-e9f1e4941b43" :question/math-academy-id "q-140953" :question/problem "Consider the system $Ax=b$, where the matrix $A$ and the vector $b$ are shown below. Given that the columns of $A$ are linearly independent, find the minimum value of $‖Ax-b‖.$\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First of all, we write the given system in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{A}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{x}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]}} & =\\overset{b}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]}} \\\\ Ax & =b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can find the least-squares solution $\\overset{^}{x}$ of the equation above by solving the corresponding normal equation, which we obtain by left-multiplying our original equation by ${A}^{T}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A\\overset{^}{x} & ={A}^{T}b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the columns of $A$ are linearly independent, the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A$ is invertible. Therefore, multiplying by $({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}$ on the left, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{^}{x} & =({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}{A}^{T}b \\\\  & ={([\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 2 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\,\\,[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 2 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={[\\begin{aligned}7 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 7\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{45}[\\begin{aligned}7 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 7\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe minimum value of $‖Ax-b‖$ is attained when $x=\\overset{^}{x},$ which is the least-squares solution of the system $Ax=b.$ In this case, $A\\overset{^}{x}$ represents the orthogonal projection of $b$ onto the column space of $A,$ and $‖A\\overset{^}{x}-b‖$ is the distance between the vector $b$ and the column space. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A\\overset{^}{x}-b & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n‖A\\overset{^}{x}-b‖=\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{0}^{2}}=\\sqrt{3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326908 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133799 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "74efec6b-6e5f-5761-a116-5c94e3fb4326" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Least-Squares Solution of a Linear System"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "125e5ea0-2d09-53c7-bf5a-6db86f01788b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{11}{20} \\\\ -\\frac{7}{20}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324136} {:answer/id #uuid "16df845b-8aca-58e3-ae92-9d86f331bce3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{13}{20} \\\\ \\frac{1}{20}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324173} {:answer/id #uuid "24d2ae87-e1f9-50af-9aa6-98e8929a2d33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{17}{20} \\\\ \\frac{3}{20}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324274} {:answer/id #uuid "b8e4ad4a-f6d5-57ac-9b52-100c6666021e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{20} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{20}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325558} {:answer/id #uuid "cf6ec109-3e58-5c22-b7fa-223132d14aab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{20} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325773}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b8e4ad4a-f6d5-57ac-9b52-100c6666021e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{20} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{20}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325558} :answer-field/id #uuid "24dd5431-2243-5962-ae01-cbb9b9be0bfc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326282}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "082f22b9-7dbc-5c7c-88d0-775a3d957e87" :question/math-academy-id "q-41776" :question/problem "Find the least-squares solution to the system of linear equations given below. You're given that the columns of the corresponding coefficient matrix are linearly independent.\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=1 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=-1 \\\\ -{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First of all, we write the given system in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n\\overset{A}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{x}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]}}=\\overset{b}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}}\n$$\n\nWe can find the least-squares solution $\\overset{^}{x}$ of the equation above by solving the corresponding normal equation, which we obtain by left-multiplying our original equation by ${A}^{T}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A\\overset{^}{x} & ={A}^{T}b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the columns of $A$ are linearly independent, the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A$ is invertible. Therefore, multiplying by $({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}$ on the left, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{^}{x} & =({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}{A}^{T}b \\\\  & ={([\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={[\\begin{aligned}6 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 14\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{40}[\\begin{aligned}7 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{20} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{20}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354410 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133848 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5924037a-ddc3-5f50-b4b0-1bd813cef255" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Distance Between a Vector to a Subspace of Solutions of a Linear System"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "59881df0-2ac6-532e-8fb9-91b698aa746f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352356} {:answer/id #uuid "6136a078-6ec6-579a-809a-d2077533b6a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352433} {:answer/id #uuid "76500562-20f2-5c7e-bdb3-4992adaf7d17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{111}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352607} {:answer/id #uuid "7917c258-2cdc-5cb9-a21d-ebdf986ccad6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{101}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352623} {:answer/id #uuid "7cb29578-9f41-5fba-9274-bad7f34afe91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{110}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352661}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7cb29578-9f41-5fba-9274-bad7f34afe91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{110}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352661} :answer-field/id #uuid "7e227d03-ecbf-552f-86b6-2f39084c0aba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354049}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "22b88813-fc85-5da7-b050-31934e04cdb3" :question/math-academy-id "q-85284" :question/problem "Consider the system $Ax=b$, where the matrix $A$ and the vector $b$ are shown below. Given that the columns of $A$ are linearly independent, find the minimum value of $‖Ax-b‖.$\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 14 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First of all, we write the given system in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{A}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{x}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]}} & =\\overset{b}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 14 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}} \\\\ Ax & =b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can find the least-squares solution $\\overset{^}{x}$ of the equation above by solving the corresponding normal equation, which we obtain by left-multiplying our original equation by ${A}^{T}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A\\overset{^}{x} & ={A}^{T}b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the columns of $A$ are linearly independent, the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A$ is invertible. Therefore, multiplying by $({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}$ on the left, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{^}{x} & =({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}{A}^{T}b \\\\  & ={([\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\,\\,[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 14 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ 15\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{15}[\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ 15\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe minimum value of $‖Ax-b‖$ is attained when $x=\\overset{^}{x},$ which is the least-squares solution of the system $Ax=b.$ In this case, $A\\overset{^}{x}$ represents the orthogonal projection of $b$ onto the column space of $A,$ and $‖A\\overset{^}{x}-b‖$ is the distance between the vector $b$ and the column space. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A\\overset{^}{x}-b & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 14 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n‖A\\overset{^}{x}-b‖=\\sqrt{{5}^{2}+(-4)^{2}+(-8)^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}=\\sqrt{110}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354439 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133800 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d23c4292-6fdd-5cba-a2e7-0f4d770b2309" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Least-Squares Solution of a Linear System Given in Matrix Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "47f733f4-12f3-5c07-8f4b-304b44459b9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352230} {:answer/id #uuid "8e2c331c-8cc2-5e5e-b4b6-de1a54f34fe1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352806} {:answer/id #uuid "c7ad2f12-4695-596d-8cec-b7f38fb28a29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ \\frac{3}{2} \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353297} {:answer/id #uuid "d2a56cfe-ee7f-5cca-9b65-eb74bde205f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ \\frac{3}{2} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353390} {:answer/id #uuid "e9c8975d-a61b-537d-897c-5fdec1b16da4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353601}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d2a56cfe-ee7f-5cca-9b65-eb74bde205f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ \\frac{3}{2} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353390} :answer-field/id #uuid "cda82a11-1d36-50fa-8ecc-f1dd1a7dc6ee" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354171}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "48fc2839-660f-57b5-b91c-b2fcd5bae103" :question/math-academy-id "q-85899" :question/problem "Given that the columns of $A$ are linearly independent, find the least-squares solution of $Ax=b$, where \n\n$\\,$ $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -4 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 4 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "First of all, we write the given system in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{A}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -4 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 4 & -2\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{x}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]}} & =\\overset{b}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}]}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can find the least-squares solution $\\overset{^}{x}$ of the equation above by solving the corresponding normal equation, which we obtain by left-multiplying our original equation by ${A}^{T}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A\\overset{^}{x} & ={A}^{T}b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the columns of $A$ are linearly independent, the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A$ is invertible. Therefore, multiplying by $({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}$ on the left, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{^}{x} & =({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}{A}^{T}b \\\\  & ={([\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 4 & -2 & 0 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -4 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 4 & -2\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 4 & -2 & 0 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={[\\begin{aligned}16 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 32 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 24\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}48 \\\\ 48 \\\\ 24\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{96}[\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}48 \\\\ 48 \\\\ 24\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ \\frac{3}{2} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382559 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133799 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "74efec6b-6e5f-5761-a116-5c94e3fb4326" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Least-Squares Solution of a Linear System"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5dc9412d-db1d-5f0b-bf46-1547fc9bc9d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382561} {:answer/id #uuid "f6ab9fcd-0d01-5a7c-a562-b332d1fa753b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382562} {:answer/id #uuid "7a397f58-508e-5d63-aeae-854fad3a6043" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382563} {:answer/id #uuid "2756ce9d-d692-57b4-88bb-5f748720577f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382564} {:answer/id #uuid "3f5b1550-1387-5406-a483-f580bc72d844" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382565}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7a397f58-508e-5d63-aeae-854fad3a6043" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382563} :answer-field/id #uuid "38cb7faf-1c5d-5786-81e1-1833c5631b56" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382560}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cbf886ad-eced-5102-99df-0e48cd09970a" :question/math-academy-id "q-85905" :question/problem "Find the least-squares solution to the system of linear equations given below. You're given that the columns of the corresponding coefficient matrix are linearly independent.\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2}=8 \\\\ 4{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3}=2 \\\\ -4{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}=2 \\\\ 4{x}_{1}-4{x}_{3}=-6\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First of all, we write the given system in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n\\overset{A}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{x}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]}}=\\overset{b}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]}}\n$$\n\nWe can find the least-squares solution $\\overset{^}{x}$ of the equation above by solving the corresponding normal equation, which we obtain by left-multiplying our original equation by ${A}^{T}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A\\overset{^}{x} & ={A}^{T}b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the columns of $A$ are linearly independent, the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A$ is invertible. Therefore, multiplying by $({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}$ on the left, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{^}{x} & =({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}{A}^{T}b \\\\  & ={([\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & 0 & 4 \\\\ -4 & 2 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 2 & -4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & 0 & 4 \\\\ -4 & 2 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 2 & -4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={[\\begin{aligned}36 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 36 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 36\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -36 \\\\ 36\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{36}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -36 \\\\ 36\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
